WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.030
Seven countries claim parts of Antarctica:

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:07.470
Argentina, Australia,
Chile, France, New Zealand,

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.750
Norway and the UK.

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.830
Some of those claims overlap.

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.370
Other countries recognise none of them.

6
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:19.990
In 1957 and the year after, scientists
from 12 countries worked there.

7
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.830
On 1 December 1959, those 12 countries
signed one treaty for everywhere south

8
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.170
of 60 degrees South.

9
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.230
Today, 58 countries are Parties.

10
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.690
So can one treaty keep
a whole continent safe?

11
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.770
Can it be enforced on ice?

12
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.230
Will rival countries ever agree?

13
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.210
In this mission, you'll find out
what the treaty system controls.

14
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.630
Then you'll weigh its
strengths against its limits,

15
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.570
and judge how sustainable it is.

16
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:53.240
Your mission: evaluate whether one
treaty can keep Antarctica safe.
